Follow-up to PR #695, under the same owner approval for .githooks/**.

That PR widened the trigger regex to (ir|datamodels|io_boundary) and the
comment above it, but left the skip message reading "skipped (no ir.py /
datamodels.py staged)". So a commit staging io_boundary.py alone would run
the check while a commit staging nothing would report a condition that had
not been the condition since the previous PR — a gate explaining itself
with the wrong rule, which is worse than terse, because someone debugging a
skip trusts the message over the regex.

Caught from the hook's own output on PR #695's commit rather than by
review. Now reads "skipped (no core dataclass file staged)", which is
scope-agnostic and cannot go stale the next time a file joins
DEFAULT_CORE_FILES — the alternation itself is already pinned to that
constant by
test_the_precommit_hook_regex_covers_every_scoped_core_file.

Verified live: the hook prints the new message when no core dataclass file
is staged.

